{
  "id": "warmup-1-ticket",
  "order": 1,
  "phase": "warmup",
  "title": "Warm-up 1: The Ticket",
  "flowLabel": "How a token works",
  "text": "The Client asks the IdP for a token to read the user's calendar and hands it to the Application. Then the Client tries to use the same slip to write to the calendar.",
  "userPresent": true,
  "request": {
    "action": "Read the user's calendar",
    "requiredScope": "calendar.read",
    "userScoped": true,
    "user": "user:alex"
  },
  "holders": {
    "client": [],
    "application": []
  },
  "beats": [
    {
      "starter": "client"
    },
    {
      "starter": "client"
    }
  ],
  "hands": {
    "client": [
      {
        "type": "token_request",
        "audience": "application",
        "scope": [
          "calendar.read"
        ],
        "pkce": true,
        "scripted": true,
        "beat": 0,
        "label": "Ask the IdP for a token: subject = the user, audience = Application, scope = calendar.read"
      },
      {
        "type": "request",
        "to": "application",
        "attach": "latest",
        "scripted": true,
        "beat": 0,
        "label": "Hand the slip to the Application and ask to read the calendar"
      },
      {
        "type": "request",
        "to": "application",
        "attach": "latest",
        "scripted": true,
        "beat": 1,
        "request": {
          "action": "Write to the user's calendar",
          "requiredScope": "calendar.write",
          "userScoped": true,
          "user": "user:alex"
        },
        "label": "Use the same slip to write to the calendar"
      }
    ],
    "application": [
      "app.accept",
      "app.reject"
    ],
    "idp": [
      "idp.issue",
      "idp.reject"
    ],
    "mcp": []
  },
  "teaches": [
    "A token is a ticket with a name (subject), a venue (audience) and a seat section (scope).",
    "Scope is what you may do. calendar.read does not cover a write."
  ],
  "covers": [
    "Gateway Auth Reference"
  ]
}
